Hi HN! I built this to make physics simulations more intuitive.<p>Example - simulating a pendulum:<p><pre><code>    from mechanics_dsl import PhysicsCompiler
    compiler = PhysicsCompiler()
    compiler.compile_dsl(r&quot;&quot;&quot;
        \system{pendulum}
        \lagrangian{\frac{1}{2} m l^2 \dot{\theta}^2 + m g l \cos(\theta)}
    &quot;&quot;&quot;)
    solution = compiler.simulate((0, 10))
</code></pre>
It automatically derives equations of motion and can generate C++&#x2F;Rust&#x2F;CUDA code.<p>Feedback welcome!
